    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d874-a1">

                <pb facs="1024" n="944" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg944"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr.
                            Wetherbee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By last mail I received your communication
                    in reference to a passport. Burmah is under the jurisdiction of the
                    consul-general at Calcutta, Hon. Robert F. Patterson, and I have forwarded your
                    correspondence as it came to me directly to him, with the hope that this might
                    save you some little time in a quest that seems to have cost you a good deal of
                    time and trouble. You will no doubt hear from Mr. Patterson very shortly after
                    you receive this.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Yours, sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton King.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
